# UI design aesthetic

Cursor shim — **canonical source:** [`docs/design/ui-aesthetic.md`](../../docs/design/ui-aesthetic.md) (also in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)).

Overlays, menus, settings, lobby, pause UI, and HUD chrome follow that guide.

## Quick reference

| Constant | Hex | Use |
|----------|-----|-----|
| `UiPalette.INK_BLACK` | `#06080f` | Deepest backdrop, scrim base |
| `UiPalette.DARK_AMETHYST` | `#261342` | Primary panel / button fill |
| `UiPalette.PRUSSIAN_BLUE` | `#14213d` | Elevated panels, nested surfaces |
| `UiPalette.HUNTER_GREEN` | `#355e3b` | Success / live / positive |
| `UiPalette.HONEY_BRONZE` | `#e2ab43` | Borders, focus, primary accent |
| `UiPalette.SNOW` | `#f6efee` | Text on dark surfaces |

Full palette data: `resources/ui/palette.json`

## Rules

- Prefer **`UiPalette`** constants and `panel_style()` / `button_style()` over hard-coded `Color(...)`.
- Overlay pattern: scrim (`SCRIM`) → centered panel (`BACKGROUND_ELEVATED` + `BORDER_DEFAULT`, 10px radius) → margins 16–20px.
- Buttons: `BACKGROUND_PRIMARY` + 2px bronze border, 8px radius; hover brightens border toward `BORDER_HOVER`.
- Do not add new menu accent colors without updating `docs/design/ui-aesthetic.md` and `palette.json`.
- World / spell / monster colors stay separate unless explicitly restyling HUD chrome.

When extending the system, update the doc, JSON, and `ui_palette.gd` together.
